## **2. Design Patterns in Chess Application**
### **A. Singleton Pattern (Rating System)**
Ensures only **one instance** of `RatingManager` exists.  

```cpp
// RatingManager.h
#pragma once
#include <mutex>
#include <map>

class RatingManager {
private:
    static RatingManager* instance;
    static std::mutex mtx;
    std::map<std::string, int> playerRatings;

    RatingManager() {} // Private constructor

public:
    static RatingManager* getInstance() {
        std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(mtx);
        if (!instance) {
            instance = new RatingManager();
        }
        return instance;
    }

    void updateRating(const std::string& player, bool won) {
        if (won) playerRatings[player]++;
        else playerRatings[player]--;
    }

    int getRating(const std::string& player) {
        return playerRatings[player];
    }
};
```

